Actually, let me think about the double-free. The crash is a heap-double-free. Let me look at the `err` label path. When `goto err` is hit, `free_context(ctx)` is called which frees all `desc[i].buf`. If two descriptors point to the same buffer (aliasing), that would cause a double-free.

In the copy path, `ctx->desc[i].buf = malloc(...)` then `memcpy(ctx->desc[i].buf, ctx->desc[j].buf, ...)`. This creates a separate copy, so no aliasing there.

